WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.231 --> 00:00:04.430
This is Hollywood makeup
wizard Kevin Yagher,

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:07.840
and these wrinkles on
his face aren't real.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.800
They were actually created
with a method called stippling,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.400
which deepens the crow's
feet around his eyes.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.100
From sculpting enlarged earlobes
to painting broken veins,

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.640
it's just one of the many
ways he can make performers

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.350
like Keanu Reeves look 95 years old.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.610
Kevin draws inspiration from many classic

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.560
old-age makeup looks and movies,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.380
but he gets much of his material

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.400
just by observing people
in the real world.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.860
When he turned Alex
Winter into Granny Preston

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.720
for "Bill and Ted's Bogus
Journey" back in 1991,

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.080
he was inspired by his mother-in-law.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.230
She had these great apple cheeks.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.770
She had that classic
granny look to her face.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.740
When he had to make
Alex and Keanu look like

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.010
they were 95 years old in
"Bill and Ted Face the Music,"

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.890
he started with these Photoshop concepts.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.640
With Keanu, I wanted to
give him an Iggy Pop,

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.810
skinnier, older, aged rocker look,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.169
and with Alex, I wanted to get him

00:00:59.169 --> 00:01:01.200
a happier, friendly disposition.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.890
Every prosthetic-related look

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.730
starts with lifecasts.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.360
Since only Alex and
Keanu's bare necks, faces,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.250
and arms were visible on camera,

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.360
Kevin didn't need prosthetics
for their entire bodies.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.160
Instead, only the actors'
heads and arms were covered

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.820
in purple and green silicone rubbers.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.730
The green silicone has an oil in it

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.290
that ensures it won't pull
any of the actors' hairs

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.750
out of their bodies.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.690
The impressions are then
wrapped in temporary plaster

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.780
to hold them together before being cast

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.363
in Hydrocal and urethane.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.870
The lifecasting process helps
a makeup artist replicate

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.360
the little details of a performer's skin.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.040
But when it came to Alex
and Keanu's old-age looks,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.020
the lifecasts also helped
Kevin find and exaggerate

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.340
wrinkles already forming on
their faces and forearms.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.750
Just kind of studied
the lines of their faces

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.380
and to see where, you
know, droopage starts.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.850
How his jowls are beginning to form,

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.590
his nasal labial folds
becoming more prominent.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.050
You know, his eye sockets
are deepening a slight bit.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.470
To mimic the fine details of old skin,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.120
he added clay to the bust

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.690
of Alex and Keanu's faces and forearms,

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:08.930
which allowed him to sculpt
directly on the skin.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.470
This was where Kevin could add wrinkles

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.170
and veins that really stick out.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.370
And different ages don't look the same.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.590
While Kevin made Alex
and Keanu look 95 here,

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.500
in the movie "Blow,"

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.680
he made Johnny Depp look just a bit older

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.730
than he already was,

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.924
aging the actor from his
late 30s into his 60s.

00:02:25.924 --> 00:02:29.060
As you can see, there
are still aged features

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.430
on his face, but less pronounced.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.100
The pores on the 95-year-old
skin look more elongated,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.700
something Kevin observed and mimicked

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.790
while creating texture.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.440
As you get older, they begin
to stretch with your skin.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.280
Kevin and his team also had to create

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.710
really pronounced
wrinkles for Bill and Ted.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.630
They achieved this by crosshatching

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.200
all over the characters'
forearms and faces,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.600
but they changed up their technique

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.120
on different parts of the body.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.600
Chin's kind of funny because it gets a lot

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.150
of weird crosshatching wrinkles in them.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.530
And wrinkles around
the eyes or crow's feet

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.290
required a different pattern too,

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.120
an effect that they could also
achieve through stippling.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.070
Stippling is done by simply
adding a latex-based liquid

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.840
to the skin and powdering it.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.360
It stretches the skin and
causes these wrinkles.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.490
Kevin used this technique
on Pete Postlethwaite

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.870
to create wrinkles around his eyes

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.320
when the actor had to play a character

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.490
who was hundreds of
years old in "Aeon Flux."

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.330
I didn't have to do any age to him

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:22.700
as far as like, accentuate all the things

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:23.550
I did to these guys.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:24.680
He already had it in his face,

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.630
but he just was wasn't old enough.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.610
The body doesn't just wrinkle as you age.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.600
When you get to be 95,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.432
your bones begin to show,
meaning your sockets get deeper.

00:03:33.432 --> 00:03:35.510
Kevin made sure bone was visible

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.030
when sculpting their hands.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.250
Because Bill and Ted were so old,

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.340
he also wanted them to look arthritic,

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.040
a trait that shows up
especially in the hands.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:44.980
You get this curved look.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.250
I can't do much about that.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.160
But what I could do is
exaggerate these knuckles.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.310
You can see a fine little
bone in between each knuckle,

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:51.610
and the knuckles are swollen.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.790
And going farther up the arm,

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.120
he even made the wrist bone stand out.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.690
Once Kevin and his team
sculpted all the details,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.670
they created another set of negatives

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.960
and then poured silicone into those molds

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.050
and sandwiched it all together.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.520
Silicone is necessary

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.360
for perfectly mimicking the translucency

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.450
and texture of skin.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.380
As you can see here,

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.880
it also naturally wrinkles
like old human skin would.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.050
The color of the silicone is
already intrinsically colored

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.070
to be a flesh tone.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.310
And then you can see light through this,

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:21.060
if I could get that at the right angle.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.410
But it's not until
additional colors are added

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.260
that all the sculpted
wrinkles and bones and pores

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.250
begin to look realistic.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.560
Kevin started with a
basic skin color palette

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.240
of green and a heavy emphasis on red.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.150
Meanwhile, the thinning hairs punched

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.280
into Keanu's head weren't a solid gray.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.900
They were actually a
mix of white and yellow.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:40.950
When looking at the eyes,

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.230
Kevin knew that the color
around the eye sockets

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:45.840
darkens with age, and
airbrushing and shadow

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.000
helps the sculpted areas really pop,

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.940
making the bone structure
much more visible.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.910
While veins are usually sculpted,

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.520
Kevin also elevated them
through airbrushing.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.040
This tool was especially helpful

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.050
for the aging veins on their faces.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.240
Like on Alex and Keanu's muscle suits,

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.710
Kevin can airbrush on details, like pores.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.020
But for their old age,

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.860
he needed to add even
more decay to the skin.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.500
These delicate imperfections,

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.380
like these purple and red capillaries

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.553
on Keanu's prosthetic nose,
needed to be painted by hand.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.530
He has to do the same with liver spots,

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.687
but they are bigger and more noticeable.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:21.940
A lot of them are tiny little breakups,

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.330
little tiny dots, like freckles.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.412
And then I most likely hand-paint

00:05:25.412 --> 00:05:26.740
all the liver spots.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.940
When you get to be bigger spots

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.010
like from some of these pieces,

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.310
I'll actually go back in and
hand-paint all the bigger ones,

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.910
and I'll place those exactly
where I want them to be.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.290
Tiny aging freckles

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.130
also make the skin look older.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.570
He found that for some of those,

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.550
he could easily get lots on at once

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.963
by taking a chip brush and flicking it.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.391
For "Face the Music,"

00:05:46.391 --> 00:05:48.340
Kevin added additional layers of makeup

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.870
to the actors that might
seem like overkill,

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.550
but they really sell the look

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.470
and bring out the kinds of aging details

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.060
you might never think of.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.860
For example, when people get older,

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.740
their noses and ears often enlarge.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.460
Kevin estimates that he had
to make Alex and Keanu's ears

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.360
and noses about 20% bigger
than their normal size.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.930
It wasn't just the skin
that had to look old.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:10.840
On "Face the Music,"

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.820
Kevin realized he could make Alex look old

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.470
by giving him cataracts.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:17.260
So Kevin used these
glassy-looking contact lenses

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.260
that gave Alex foggy eyes.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.540
Now, if they were too opaque,
Alex would have looked blind,

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.240
while cataracts have more of a milky look.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.880
Old man, young man. Well, almost young.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:30.980
Old, sort of young, old, kind of old.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:32.800
And by using a simple combo

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.410
of glue and thickener,

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.362
he could apply fake eye
bags to Keanu on set.

00:06:37.362 --> 00:06:39.740
They're like stickers almost,
and you just put them down.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.250
Then you kind of blend the edges quicker.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.230
The attention to both the big details

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.300
and especially all those little ones

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.490
that only an artist
could think of surprised

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.283
even the actors themselves.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.310
Throughout several decades
of doing old-age makeup,

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.260
Kevin has found the key
to getting it right,

00:06:58.260 --> 00:06:59.730
knowing that it's imperfect.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.850
The great thing about old-age makeups

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.000
is that mistakes are welcome.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.833
They're messy, and they're flawed.

